From cab284d1cf97d131c6332e7d9164504a41b2f829 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hi3798 port <port@localhost>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:02:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: hisilicon: zero the reset controller struct before
 registering

hisi_reset_init() allocates struct hisi_reset_controller with devm_kmalloc()
and then fills in only five fields of the embedded reset_controller_dev:
owner, ops, of_node, of_reset_n_cells and of_xlate. Everything else keeps
whatever was in the heap.

That was survivable until the reset core grew fwnode support. It now rejects
a controller that supplies both an of_node and an fwnode:

	if ((rcdev->of_node && rcdev->fwnode) ||
	    (rcdev->of_xlate && rcdev->fwnode_xlate))
		return -EINVAL;

rcdev->fwnode and rcdev->fwnode_xlate are uninitialised here, so registration
fails whenever the garbage happens to be non-NULL.

hisi_reset_init() ignores the return value, so nothing is logged. The
controller is simply absent from reset_controller_list, and every consumer
that names it resolves to -EPROBE_DEFER and defers forever -- silently, since
deferred probe prints nothing. On Hi3798MV200/MV300 that takes out both MMC
controllers and the watchdog:

	f8a2c000.watchdog	sp805-wdt: Can not get reset
	f9820000.mmc		dwmmc_hi3798mv200: parse dt failed
	f9830000.mmc		dwmmc_hi3798mv200: parse dt failed

Consumers that reach further into the reset core fare worse. rcdev->dev is
uninitialised too, and dwc3-of-simple dereferences it:

	Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address a1ff001470cd984e
	pc : kobject_get	lr : get_device
	  __fwnode_reset_control_get
	  fwnode_reset_control_array_get
	  dwc3_of_simple_probe
	Kernel panic - not syncing: Attempted to kill init!

Use devm_kzalloc(), and stop discarding the registration error so a future
failure is visible instead of appearing as an unexplained deferred probe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/hisilicon/reset.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/hisilicon/reset.c b/drivers/clk/hisilicon/reset.c
index 93cee17db8b1..90d9eb372cbe 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/hisilicon/reset.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/hisilicon/reset.c
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ struct hisi_reset_controller *hisi_reset_init(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct hisi_reset_controller *rstc;
 
-	rstc = devm_kmalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*rstc), GFP_KERNEL);
+	rstc = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*rstc), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!rstc)
 		return NULL;
 
@@ -105,7 +105,8 @@ struct hisi_reset_controller *hisi_reset_init(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	rstc->rcdev.of_node = pdev->dev.of_node;
 	rstc->rcdev.of_reset_n_cells = 2;
 	rstc->rcdev.of_xlate = hisi_reset_of_xlate;
-	reset_controller_register(&rstc->rcdev);
+	if (reset_controller_register(&rstc->rcdev))
+		return NULL;
 
 	return rstc;
 }
